session:
  updated: 2026-07-28
  status: thin_slice_complete
  branch: feat/portable-context-router

goal:
  current: deliver the portable context router thin slice

completed:
  - added a TOON reader/writer for control files (Task 1)
  - added a profile config and deterministic precedence resolver (Task 2)
  - added runtime detection and contract fingerprinting (Task 3)
  - added observations with invalidation and bounded escalation (Task 4)
  - added skill catalog resolution and taxonomy layer discovery (Task 5)
  - added task-risk classification and context plan assembly (Task 6)
  - added `project context explain` and `project context observe` (Task 7)
  - added taxonomy, router config and canonical-source validation (Task 8)
  - added fixture-scored capability qualification — unguessable, defeat score 0 of 6 blind (Task 9)
  - migrated context-packet into taxonomy layers and removed duplicated rules (Task 10)
  - migrated review-loop into five taxonomy layers (Task 11)
  - separated wiki methodology from product with axis enforcement (Task 12)
  - added `project context scaffold` and the generated-project fixture (Task 13)
  - added the acceptance suite (AC-1 to AC-14), `context test` and CI integration (Task 14)
  - documented the router, recorded decisions and updated handoff (Task 15)
  - addressed all review findings (B1, B2, B3, D1, D2, D3, D4)

in_progress: []

next:
  - open a PR for feat/portable-context-router into main
  - try the scaffold on a real existing project to surface adoption friction
  - Phase 1: slim AGENTS.md and promote remaining candidate topics (D1, D2, D4, D8, D9)
  - Phase 1: migrate remaining skills into taxonomy layers
  - promote INBOX-009 after a real generated project reports profile-based preloading improves quality

decisions:
  - id: portable_context_router
    summary: route context depth and timing by profile, never required behaviour
  - id: capability_by_observation_not_registry
    summary: license lean context from fixture-scored behaviour, never from model identity
  - id: wiki_method_product_axis
    summary: every wiki page declares axis method or product, matching its directory
  - id: yaml_skill_frontmatter_deviation
    summary: keep skill frontmatter in YAML despite the TOON default for state

risks:
  - the router's only evidence is the template's own fixture; promotion needs a real generated project
  - project check still warns on D1, D2, D4, D8, D9 — the Phase 1 dedupe ledger
  - no independent review round was run; the test suite and context checks provide the deterministic gate
  - context-test was added back to SCAFFOLD_COPY after Task 14 created it

